-- title:
--   A node package over a larger coefficient field
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $N$ is a positive integer, $k$ is an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ is a ring homomorphism. Further fixed are: a modular polynomial datum `data` for $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ vanishing at $(j, j_q)$), the Kronecker congruence `hKr` for it (the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ is the product of $\mathrm{C}(X)^{q} - X$ and $\mathrm{C}(X) - X^{q}$), the integrality hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` stating that the two degeneracy embeddings $\bar\alpha, \bar\beta$ of the level-$N$ function field into the level-$Nq$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are integral ring maps, and a place specialisation $P$ of the level-$N$ curve at $A$ (the datum of a map `P.sp` from places of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(N))$, realised as `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, to places of the characteristic-$q$ function field `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, a homomorphism on degree-zero divisor classes, and compatibility laws for the $j$-coordinates). It is assumed that $q \nmid N$ (`hqN`).
--
--   The finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` over $k$ is required, by `hW`, to consist exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q N k`: those $w$ that are rational, at which both $j$ and $j_N$ are regular, and whose $j$-value is a supersingular $j$-invariant. $R$ is a prolongation tuple for $P$, i.e. a pair of regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to the level-$Nq$ function field together with the residue-field data $\overline{\mathrm{red}}$, $\iota$ and the Atkin–Lehner compatibilities. Four laws are imposed on $R$: `hR` ($R$ is a model: the two divisor laws computing the pushforwards along `P.reduceFst`, `P.reduceSnd` of the divisor of a function in terms of the orders of its two residues, at places not fixed by the square of the Frobenius map on places, and the two cusp laws on the infinity and zero sides); `hRL` (the regularity law over $W$, in two clauses: non-negativity of the orders of both residues at affine geometric places fixed by the square of Frobenius, and existence of a common value of the two residues at each node pair of $W$); `hNV` (the node value law over $W$: for a function with nonzero residues and no zero or pole above a node pair, the two residues take a common nonzero value at the two members of the pair); and `hO` (the fixed-order law: for $f$ integral for $R_1$ and $R_2$ with nonzero residues and $D$ the divisor of $f$, at every affine geometric place $v$ fixed by the square of the Frobenius map on places, the multiplicity of $v$ in the pushforward of $D$ along `P.reduceFst` equals $\mathrm{ord}_v$ of the first residue plus $\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{Frob}\,v}$ of the second residue).
--
--   Finally, `dat` is a level-$N$ annulus datum for $R$ over $W$: it assigns to each place $w$ a coefficient field `dat.K w` intermediate between $\mathbb{Q}$ and $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, to each $w \in W$ a pair of node coordinates `dat.coord w hw` (elements $x, y$ of the node ring `R.nodeIntegersOver (dat.K w) w` with first residue of $x$ zero, order $1$ of the second residue of $x$ at the Frobenius translate of $w$, second residue of $y$ zero and order $1$ of the first residue of $y$ at $w$), a width `dat.width w`, and further fields `depthQ`, `unifFst`, `unifSnd`, `corrFst`, `corrSnd` and units `u0`, `lam`, `mu` of $k$. Here `NodeLocalized.coeffSubring A K` is the subring $A \cap K$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, `NodeLocalized.redRestrict red K` is the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to it, `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` is the ring of those elements of the level-$Nq$ function field that are integral for $R_1$, for $R_2$ and at every place $V$ of that field with `P.reduceFst V = w`, and whose $q$-expansion lies in the subfield `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K` generated by the constants of $K$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$, and `R.nodeConst K w` is the constant embedding $A \cap K \to$ `R.nodeIntegersOver K w`.
--
--   The presentation hypotheses at the places of $W$ are as follows. Widths are at least $1$ (`hwidth`); every `dat.K w` is finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, for all places $w$ (`hK`). Given are families $\varpi$, $\varepsilon$ of elements of $A \cap$ `dat.K w`, a family of natural numbers $eK$, and for $w \in W$ a unit candidate $u$ in the node ring over `dat.K w`, subject to: $\varpi_w$ generates the kernel of the reduction on $A \cap$ `dat.K w`, in the sense that `redRestrict red (dat.K w) d = 0` if and only if $d$ is a multiple of $\varpi_w$ (`hϖ`); $eK_w \ge 1$ (`heK`); $\varepsilon_w$ is a unit (`hε`); $q = \varpi_w^{eK_w}\varepsilon_w$ in $A \cap$ `dat.K w` (`hqϖ`); $u_w$ is a unit of the node ring and $x\,y = (\text{const }\varpi_w)^{\,\mathrm{width}(w)\cdot eK_w}\,u_w$ for the node coordinates at $w$ (`hu`); the ideal generated by $\text{const }\varpi_w$, $x$ and $y$ is maximal and is the unique maximal ideal of the node ring (`hmax`); the two branch ideals generated by $\text{const }\varpi_w$ together with $x$, respectively $y$, are prime, with $y$ outside the first and $x$ outside the second (`hbr`); the node ring is Noetherian (`hnoeth`); every element $g$ of the node ring satisfies $g - \text{const}\,o$ is a non-unit for some $o \in A \cap$ `dat.K w` (`hres`); and the first residue `R.nodeResidue₁ w` of $u_w$ has value `dat.u0 w` at $w$ in the sense of `Place.HasValue` (`hu0`). Lastly, `hker` asserts that the kernel of $\mathrm{red}$ is the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Input data for the conclusion: a place $w \in W$, a nonzero element $f$ of the level-$Nq$ function field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, and two nonzero scalars $c_1, c_2 \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   The assertion is the existence of an intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ with `dat.K w` $\le K'$ and $K'$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, an inclusion of node rings `R.nodeIntegersOver (dat.K w) w` $\le$ `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w`, elements $\varpi'$, $\varepsilon'$, $\eta_1$, $\eta_2$, $\nu$ of $A \cap K'$, natural numbers $eK'$ and $r$, an element $u'$ of `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w`, integers $m_1, m_2$, and units $u_0'$, $t$, $\bar\varepsilon'$ of $k$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   First, $\varpi'$ generates the kernel of reduction on $A \cap K'$: `redRestrict red K' d = 0` if and only if $d$ is a multiple of $\varpi'$. Second, $eK' \ge 1$, $\varepsilon'$ is a unit, and $q = \varpi'^{\,eK'}\varepsilon'$ in $A \cap K'$. Third, $u'$ is a unit of `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w` and, as an identity in the level-$Nq$ function field, $x\,y = (\text{const}_{K'}\varpi')^{\,\mathrm{width}(w)\cdot eK'}\,u'$, where $x$, $y$ are the coordinates `dat.coord w hw`. Fourth, the ideal of `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w` generated by $\text{const}_{K'}\varpi'$ and the images of $x$ and $y$ under the inclusion of node rings is maximal, and every maximal ideal of `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w` equals it. Fifth, `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w` is a local ring, it is Noetherian, and its maximal ideal is exactly that ideal. Sixth, the two branch ideals generated by $\text{const}_{K'}\varpi'$ together with the image of $x$, respectively of $y$, are prime, with the image of $y$ not in the first and the image of $x$ not in the second. Seventh, for every $g$ in `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w` there is $o \in A \cap K'$ with $g - \text{const}_{K'}o$ a non-unit.
--
--   Eighth, the $q$-expansion of $f$ lies in `NodeLocalized.fieldOver (N * q) K'`, and every $z$ in that field is a quotient of two elements of the node ring over $K'$: there are elements $x_0, y_0$ of the level-$Nq$ function field, both lying in `R.nodeIntegersOver K' w`, with $y_0 \neq 0$ and $z\,y_0 = x_0$ as Laurent series. Ninth, $c_1$ and $c_2$ lie in $K'$ and factor as $c_1 = \varpi'^{\,m_1}\eta_1$ and $c_2 = \varpi'^{\,m_2}\eta_2$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $\eta_1$, $\eta_2$ units of $A \cap K'$.
--
--   Tenth, the first residue `R.nodeResidue₁ w` of $u'$ has value $u_0'$ at $w$, and $u_0' =$ `dat.u0 w` $\cdot\, t^{\,\mathrm{width}(w)\cdot eK_w}$ in $k$. Eleventh, `redRestrict red K' ε'` equals $\bar\varepsilon'$ and also equals $t^{\,eK_w}\cdot$ `redRestrict red (dat.K w) (ε w)`. Twelfth, $\nu$ is a unit of $A \cap K'$, the ramification indices are related by $eK' = r\cdot eK_w$, and in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ one has $\varpi_w = \varpi'^{\,r}\nu$ and $\varepsilon' = \nu^{\,eK_w}\varepsilon_w$. Finally, the reduction of $\nu$ is the chosen unit $t$: `redRestrict red K' ν = t`.
--
--   This is the coefficient-field enlargement step in the local analysis of the supersingular nodes of $X_0(Nq)$ in characteristic $q$, where the special fibre consists of two copies of $X_0(N)$ crossing at the supersingular points: the crossing presentation of the node ring at a supersingular place $w$, given over the coefficient field `dat.K w`, is transported to a finite extension $K'$ that in addition carries the expansion coefficients of a prescribed function $f$ and two prescribed nonzero scalars, with explicit bookkeeping of how the uniformiser, the ramification index, the unit $\varepsilon$ and the node value $u_0$ change under the enlargement. It feeds the derivation of the end-order inequality and of the coupled sheet scalings at $w$.
